SUMMARY:POSTPONED: New Wave Artist Residency panel discussion (Art in Public Places)
LOCATION:Auditorium\, 3rd floor\, Mandel Public Library of West Palm Beach\, 411 Clematis Street\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33401
CATEGORIES:City events,Arts
DESCRIPTION:Postponed due to weather; new date TBA. Source: City email 'Update: 111726 - AiPP Speaker Cancelled' (Nov 17\, 2026); City news release 'Weather forces New Wave Artist Residency Panel Discussion Postponement' (published 2026-11-17\, retrieved 2026-11-18): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111726-AiPP-Speaker-Cancelled The City of West Palm Beach's Art in Public Places (AiPP) program hosts a panel discussion presented by New Wave Artist Residency: "Art in Public Places: How Public Art Commissions Transform Artistic Practice." Designed as a lunch-and-learn for artists\, art advocates\, and community members. Panelists: artist José Alvarez (D.O.P.A.)\, whose installation Surround Me with Your Love (May All Beings Be Happy and Free)\, 2026 was commissioned by AiPP and is on exhibit at The Urban\; South Florida artists Lauren Shapiro and Laura Tanner Graham. Moderator: Amanda Sanfilippo Long\, Curator and Artist Manager for Miami-Dade County's Art in Public Places program. Schedule: 11:30 a.m. arrivals\, coffee and light bites\; noon introductory remarks and panel discussion\; 1 p.m. artist-led art tour and boxed to-go lunch\, including a walkthrough of The Urban with José Alvarez\; 2 p.m. event concludes. Registration listed on the news release: https://www.eventcreate.com/e/new-wave-art-in-public-places-panel-discussion Source: City email "Update: 111226 AiPP Hosts Season Kick-Off for New Wave Artist Residency" (Nov 12\, 2026)\; City of West Palm Beach news release "City Art in Public Places Hosts Kick-Off for New Wave Artist Residency" (published 2026-11-12\, retrieved 2026-11-13): https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-AiPP-Hosts-Season-Kick-Off-for-New-Wave-Artist-Residency
URL:https://www.wpb.org/News-Folder/News-2026/111226-AiPP-Hosts-Season-Kick-Off-for-New-Wave-Artist-Residency
END:VEVENT
