DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261228T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261228T130000
SUMMARY:Animal Olympics
LOCATION:Grassy Waters Preserve Nature Center\, 8264 Northlake Blvd\, West Palm Beach\, FL 33412
CATEGORIES:City events
DESCRIPTION:Join Grassy Waters Preserve naturalists to learn about the amazing adaptations of Everglades animals. Learn about these adaptations by competing through a series of hands-on activities to find out if you have what it takes to be an Everglades animal. Can you see as well as an owl? Are you as long as an alligator? Can you reach as far as a heron\, and more. Monday\, December 28\, 2026. Come anytime between 10:00 a.m.–1:00 p.m. Ages: All ages (with participating adult). Cost: FREE. Come prepared: This will be an indoor program. No Reservations Required. Source: City email "Grassy Waters Film Screening & December Programs" (received Nov 19\, 2026)\; Public Program Calendar (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar\; program page (retrieved 2026-11-20): https://www.wpb.org/Departments/Grassy-Waters-Preserve/Public-Program-Calendar/Animal-Olympics-122826
